{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789226051,"nonce":"a++MM1zV2RidClqnRpTxfNopz0E=","title":"An extern's link name is registered only when it is lowered, so earlier call sites box its argument twice","message":"`extern_link_names` is filled in `lower_function` as each extern is\nreached. A function lowered before the extern's declaration therefore\ndoes not know the callee is a runtime symbol: the call site coerces the\nargument to the declared `Any` parameter with `zyntax_box_*`, and the\nbackend, which does know the symbol's registered dynamic signature,\nboxes the resulting pointer again. The callee reads a box holding a\nbox and prints an address.\n\nReproducer (Python frontend, whose builtins are declared after the\nprogram's own functions): `print(int(True))` printed a pointer;\n`print(len(\"abc\"))` was right only because a string is already a\npointer. Declaration order was the whole difference.\n\nThe same order dependence made the W0001 \"no type annotation\" warning\nfire for every extern with an untyped parameter, where the registered\nsignature is the type.\n\nFix: register the link name in the declaration pre-pass, beside the\nparameter and return types; the SSA treats any callee with a link name\nas marshalled by the backend; the warning skips externs with a link\nname.","files":null}]}